   "hash": "d9044688",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.1#p1-d9044688",
     "text": "As coverings for the ark, the candlestick, the altars and such like.",
     "label": "a",
     "anchor": "cloths of service"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/EXO.39.6",
   "range": "EXO.39.6",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "e0a297e3",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.6#p1-e0a297e3",
     "text": "That is, of very fine and curious workmanship.",
     "label": "b",
     "anchor": "signets are graven"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/EXO.39.12",
   "range": "EXO.39.12",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "dd40b41e",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.12#p1-dd40b41e",
     "text": "Or, a turkeis, a stone which the authors write comes from the urine of the Lynx.",
     "label": "c",
     "anchor": "a ligure"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/EXO.39.14",
   "range": "EXO.39.14",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "964d0067",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.14#p1-964d0067",
     "text": "That is, every tribe had his name written on a stone.",
     "label": "d",
     "anchor": "according to their names"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/EXO.39.22",
   "range": "EXO.39.22",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "f8746c59",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.22#p1-f8746c59",
     "text": "Which was next under the Ephod.",
     "label": "e",
     "anchor": "ephod of woven work"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/EXO.39.23",
   "range": "EXO.39.23",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "84d36090",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.23#p1-84d36090",
     "text": "Where he could put his head through.",
     "label": "f",
     "anchor": "there was an hole in the"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/EXO.39.34",
   "range": "EXO.39.34",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "2c00fdfb",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.34#p1-2c00fdfb",
     "text": "So called, because it hung before the mercyseat and covered it from sight Ex 35:12.",
     "label": "g",
     "anchor": "vail of the covering",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Ex 35:12",
       "ref": "EXO.35.12"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/EXO.39.37",
   "range": "EXO.39.37",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "efa587e1",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.37#p1-efa587e1",
     "text": "Or, which Aaron dressed and refreshed with oil every morning Ex 30:7.",
     "label": "h",
     "anchor": "set in order",
     "refs": [
      {
       "text": "Ex 30:7",
       "ref": "EXO.30.7"
      }
     ]
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/EXO.39.42",
   "range": "EXO.39.42",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "ae115ea0",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.42#p1-ae115ea0",
     "text": "Signifying that in God's matters man may neither add, nor diminish.",
     "label": "i",
     "anchor": "commanded Moses"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "geneva/EXO.39.43",
   "range": "EXO.39.43",
   "kind": "passage",
   "hash": "6e360d93",
   "paragraphs": [
    {
     "id": "geneva/EXO.39.43#p1-6e360d93",
     "text": "Praised God for the peoples diligence and prayed for them.",
     "label": "k",
     "anchor": "blessed them"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}
